Note: The range(8) line defines the range of planet indices from 0 to 7, which corresponds to the 8 planets in our solar system. The if planet == planet1 or planet == planet2: line ensures that we only consider planets that are not planet1 or planet2. The distance = math.hypot(planet1[0] - planet2[0], planet1[1] - planet2[1]) line calculates the distance between planet1 and planet2, and the if distance < math.hypot(planet1[0] - planet1[0], planet1[1] - planet1[1]): line checks if the distance between planet1 and planet2 is less than the distance between planet1 and its own center. If it is, then we consider planet to be closer to planet1 than planet2. Finally, the yield planet line adds planet to the tuple return value.

